{%- comment -%}
  kit-price-math
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Every money figure on the kit template derives from the referenced
  products' live prices. Nothing here is typed, stored, or editable —
  a component price change updates the buy box, the savings section
  and the other-kits cards with no manual edit.

  Because {% render %} runs in its own scope, a snippet cannot assign
  variables for its caller. This one ECHOES its result instead, as a
  pipe-delimited string the caller captures and splits.

  Usage:
    {%- capture kit_math -%}
      {%- render 'kit-price-math', kit: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign math = kit_math | strip | split: '|' -%}
    {%- assign separate_total = math[0] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign kit_price      = math[1] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign saved          = math[2] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign saved_pct      = math[3] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign saved_annual   = math[4] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign counted        = math[5] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign missing        = math[6] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign is_override    = math[7] | plus: 0 -%}

  Fields, all money in cents so the money filter can format them:
    0 separate_total  sum of component product prices
    1 kit_price       the kit's own price
    2 saved           separate_total - kit_price, floored at 0
    3 saved_pct       saved as a whole percent of separate_total
    4 saved_annual    saved * 12
    5 counted         components that resolved to a price
    6 missing         components that did not resolve
    7 is_override     1 when custom.compare_at_total supplied the total

  MISSING DATA. A component with no product reference, or one whose
  product carries no price, cannot contribute to the sum. Counting
  those in `missing` lets the caller suppress a total that would be
  understated rather than print a wrong saving — a claim about money
  is not a figure to guess at. Callers must check it.

  Params:
    kit  — the product to compute for. Defaults to the page product,
           so section 09 can pass each related kit in turn.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign kit_product = kit | default: product

  assign separate_total = 0
  assign counted = 0
  assign missing = 0
  assign is_override = 0

  assign components = kit_product.metafields.custom.kit_components.value

  for component in components
    assign component_product = component.product.value

    comment
      A price of zero is indistinguishable from an unresolved one here,
      and both are equally unusable as a sum, so both count as missing.
    endcomment
    if component_product != blank and component_product.price > 0
      assign separate_total = separate_total | plus: component_product.price
      assign counted = counted | plus: 1
    else
      assign missing = missing | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    The override exists for a kit holding something that is not sold on
    its own, where summing the components cannot reach the real
    separate price. It is never the default path — only an explicit
    value replaces the computed sum.
  endcomment
  assign override = kit_product.metafields.custom.compare_at_total.value.amount
  if override > 0
    assign separate_total = override | times: 100 | round
    assign is_override = 1
    assign missing = 0
  endif

  assign kit_price = kit_product.price | default: 0

  assign saved = 0
  assign saved_pct = 0
  assign saved_annual = 0

  comment
    Only a total above the kit price is a saving. A stale or absent
    compare figure would otherwise produce a negative "saving", which
    reads as a price rise.
  endcomment
  if separate_total > kit_price and kit_price > 0
    assign saved = separate_total | minus: kit_price
    assign saved_annual = saved | times: 12

    comment
      100.0, not 100: divided_by on two integers truncates, so a 25%
      saving divides out to 24.98 and would read as 24%.
    endcomment
    assign saved_pct = saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: separate_total | round
  endif
-%}
{{- separate_total }}|{{ kit_price }}|{{ saved }}|{{ saved_pct }}|{{ saved_annual }}|{{ counted }}|{{ missing }}|{{ is_override -}}
